  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "7bf3df8c-2f95-46aa-9dc7-6efaeefb21a3",
    "name": "Tic-Tac-Toe Real-Time Game API",
    "description": "Comprehensive Postman collection for testing the authoritative 1-vs-1 Tic-Tac-Toe backend API.\n\n### Authentication\nAuthentication is handled via the HTTP-only cookie `game-session`. Postman automatically stores and passes cookies back on subsequent requests when executing `POST /api/v1/session`.\n\n### Room Lifecycle & Socket Integration\n1. **Room Creation / Joining (REST)**:\n   - `POST /api/v1/rooms` creates a room (Player 1).\n   - `POST /api/v1/rooms/:code/join` adds Player 2 to the room and starts the 3-second countdown.\n2. **Socket.IO Real-Time Channel**:\n   - Sockets authenticate via the `game-session` cookie during the handshake.\n   - Client emits `room:join` with `{ \"code\": \"...\" }` to associate the socket connection with their room channel and restore state (this does not add a new player).\n   - Real-time game interactions (moves, 30s turn timer, 60s reconnect grace, 30s rematch request expiration) use Socket.IO events as documented in README.md.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
