    {
      "name": "Session",
      "description": "Endpoints for player session initialization and restoration.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create or Restore Session",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"Status code is 200 or 201\", function () {",
                  "    pm.expect(pm.response.code).to.be.oneOf([200, 201]);",
                  "});",
                  "",
                  "pm.test(\"Response has success envelope\", function () {",
                  "    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.eql(true);",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('playerId');",
                  "    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('name');",
                  "});"
                ],
                "type": "text/javascript"
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"Mohyddine\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/v1/session",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "v1",
                "session"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a new player session or restores an existing one if the `game-session` cookie is present.\n\n- **Request body with a valid player name is required when creating a session.**\n- Names must be 2–20 characters containing only letters, numbers, and spaces; capitalization is preserved.\n- Missing or invalid names return `400 INVALID_NAME`.\n- If two players named `John` join the same room, their room display names are `John` and `John2`; both stored `name` values remain `John`.\n- Sets the `game-session` HTTP-only cookie."
          },
          "response": [
            {
